{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/developing-today/code/pulls/14906","id":5486666699,"node_id":"PR_kwDOJWP4788AAAABRwfjyw","html_url":"https://github.com/developing-today/code/pull/14906","diff_url":"https://github.com/developing-today/code/pull/14906.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/developing-today/code/pull/14906.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/developing-today/code/issues/14906","commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/developing-today/code/pulls/14906/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/developing-today/code/pulls/14906/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/developing-today/code/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/developing-today/code/issues/14906/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/developing-today/code/statuses/55527e07dff852861f9b6141f8c7b5ee9d3b7bf2","number":14906,"state":"closed","locked":false,"title":"fleet search: add the backup verb (atlas-backup port, #14129)","user":{"login":"developing-today-fleet[bot]","id":352462551,"node_id":"BOT_kgDOFQIm1w","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/26439447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/developing-today-fleet%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/developing-today-fleet","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/developing-today-fleet%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/developing-today-fleet%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/developing-today-fleet%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/developing-today-fleet%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/developing-today-fleet%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/developing-today-fleet%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/developing-today-fleet%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/developing-today-fleet%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/developing-today-fleet%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"Refs #14129 (slice of #5670 §8) — the backup verb lands; the issue stays open for the unit switch-over, one nightly cycle on the fleet path, retiring the outside copies, and the #5670 update.\n\n## What this is\n\n`fleet search backup` — a faithful port of the live `atlas-backup` shell routine (`nixos/home/atlas-backup.sh`) into the fleet binary:\n\n- snapshots the canonical local atlas.db consistently (`sqlite3 .backup`), gzips deterministically (mtime 0, no stored name), files the **same bytes** to the laptop backups root, R2 (`supabase-backups` / `atlas/<DATE>/…`), and Google Drive (`Cloud/cold-store/db-backups/local-atlas/`)\n- sha256-verified at every destination; the shell original's manifest shape, dedupe against `backup-log.md`, rotation (newest 7 dates laptop + R2, newest 4 archives on Drive), verdict/log line formats, and exit codes are unchanged, so the systemd unit and anything scraping them keep the same contract\n- R2 credentials from Bitwarden Secrets Manager at runtime, by key name only, never logged; the Drive leg uses the laptop's existing rclone `drive` remote\n\nDeliberate differences, all mechanical (also recorded in the module docs): the probe (integrity check, row counts, hashes, manifest) runs in-process instead of through the shell original's embedded Python step, so the verb needs `sqlite3`/`rclone`/`bws` but not `python3`; gzip bytes come from flate2, so the first verb run's archive hash differs from the shell original's even for an unchanged DB (one non-deduped upload, then dedupe is self-consistent); paths/tools accept `ATLAS_BACKUP_*` env overrides (defaults = the shell original's values) so the contract test can run the verb against stub tools.\n\nAlso in this PR: the fleet-registry search inventory gains `backup`, and the Fleet Book's search reference documents the verb.\n\n## Premise evidence (from #14129)\n\n- Copy reconciliation (recorded by the prior lane, comment 7123982770): the nix copy is the live one; `~/tmp/atlas-backup.sh` is gone; the hatch-personal Python copy is the outside copy to retire once the unit switches.\n- The timer run the prior park waited to observe has now happened — and failed like the one before: `atlas-backup.service` started 2026-11-24 04:58:20 CST, killed 06:28:20 CST, `Result: timeout` (identical to 2026-11-23). The shell backup times out nightly; the verb is the fix path.\n\n## Verification\n\nRoute: laptop worktree off the existing clone (named fallback — CI runs on main only; a fleet Actions exec session was started but its runner cannot reach this repo's branch, the recorded no-cross-repo-credentials gap, so it was closed unused).\n\n- `cargo test -p fleet-search` — 30 lib tests + 2 doc/other suites, all pass; includes the new backup unit tests (MD5 vs the RFC 1321 vectors, calendar validation, dedupe-log parsing per the shell rule, deterministic-gzip header) and `tests/backup_contract.rs`: the verb end-to-end against stub `sqlite3`/`bws`/`rclone`, asserting identical sha256 at all three destinations, the manifest fields, the OK/UNCHANGED verdicts and log lines, and rotation to the newest 7 laptop dates. The contract oracle is the shell script's documented behaviour.\n- `cargo test -p fleet-registry` — pass.\n- `cargo check -p fleet --features search,search-serve` — pass.\n- `cargo fmt --check` on the touched crates — clean.\n\n<!-- pm-metadata:start -->\n```json\n{\n  \"direct_parent\": null,\n  \"links\": [],\n  \"lineage\": {\n    \"design\": null,\n    \"roadmap_item\": null,\n    \"priority\": null\n  },\n  \"pm_meta\": 1,\n  \"provenance\": {\n    \"queue_id\": null,\n    \"scheduled_start\": null,\n    \"picked_up_at\": null,\n    \"work_started_at\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-11-25T06:53:28Z\",\n    \"session_id\": null,\n    \"lane\": null,\n    \"host\": \"htch-runtime\",\n    \"worktree\": null,\n    \"model\": null,\n    \"lane_start_issues\": [],\n    \"workspace_ref\": null,\n    \"auth_subject\": \"archer\",\n    \"stamped_by\": \"fleet 0.1.0 (native)\"\n  }\n}\n```\n<!-- pm-metadata:end -->\n\n<!-- codesmith:footer -->\n---\n<sup><a href=\"https://app.blacksmith.sh/developing-today/codesmith/code/pr/14906?autoLogin=true&ref=codesmith_pr_footer\">Open in [code]smith</a> · Need help on this PR? Tag <code>@codesmith-bot</code> with what you need.</sup>\n\n<!-- codesmith:autofix:disabled -->\n<!-- /codesmith:footer -->","labels":[],"milestone":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"created_at":"2026-11-25T06:53:32Z","updated_at":"2026-11-25T06:53:59Z","closed_at":"2026-11-25T06:53:57Z","merged_at":"2026-11-25T06:53:57Z","merge_commit_sha":"4532657ef73c674536745a3d1e9cc0a9c08bba1c","assignee":null,"assignees":[],"requested_reviewers":[],"requested_teams":[],"head":{"label":"developing-today:queue/iw288-14129-atlas-backup-verb","ref":"queue/iw288-14129-atlas-backup-verb","repo":{"id":627308783,"node_id":"R_kgDOJWP47w","name":"code","full_name":"developing-today/code","owner":{"login":"developing-today","id":26439447,"node_id":"MDEyOk9yZ2FuaXphdGlvbjI2NDM5NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/26439447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/developing-today","html_url":"https://github.com/developing-today","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/developing-today/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/developing-today/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/developing-today/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/developing-today/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/developing-today/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/developing-today/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/developing-today/repos","event